  "answer": "To reduce the risk of excessive absorption losses (which result in useful light being lost) in multi-layer optics, it has been proposed to deploy MP-DQN with exponential reward and Lagrangian regularisation for multi-layer optical system design (https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.05769). This is achieved through the mechanism of an MP-DQN architecture that uses separate g and f networks, where the g network proposes a thickness for each material and the f network evaluates Q-values for each material-thickness pair as well as a terminate action (https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.05769)."
